# Offer PDFs are served straight from apps/web/public and their byte offsets
# matter: a PDF carries an xref table of absolute file positions, so any
# end-of-line conversion shifts every offset and breaks the file. Git normally
# detects binaries by their NUL bytes, but an uncompressed, ASCII-only PDF has
# none and gets classified as text — which, with core.autocrlf=true, means a
# fresh clone checks out a corrupted document.
*.pdf binary
